---
/**
 * filosofia del proyecto.
 *
 * La distincion FACT / DERIVED / UNKNOWN no es decoracion: es la regla real del
 * nucleo DF-Chronicles. Aqui se explica sin vender capacidades de IA, que
 * quedan para una fase posterior.
 *
 * Accesibilidad: cada estado lleva etiqueta de texto, el color de la muestra es
 * solo un refuerzo (no depender exclusivamente del color).
 */
const states = [
  {
    key: 'fact',
    name: 'Fact',
    body: 'Recorded in the history file. Shown as it is.',
  },
  {
    key: 'derived',
    name: 'Derived',
    body: 'Computed from recorded data, and labelled as derived.',
  },
  {
    key: 'unknown',
    name: 'Unknown',
    body: 'Not recorded. Shown as a gap, never guessed.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="philosophy" aria-labelledby="philosophy-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Philosophy</p>
      <h2 id="philosophy-heading">Built from the world’s history</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="philosophy-panel">
      <blockquote>
        DF Legends is built around the historical data produced by Dwarf Fortress,
        keeping recorded facts separate from derived information and unknowns.
      </blockquote>

      <ul class="legend">
        {
          states.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <span class={`swatch swatch--${s.key}`} aria-hidden="true" />
              <span>
                <b>{s.name}</b>
                {s.body}
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <p class="philosophy-note">
        That separation is enforced in the core, not just described here. It is
        the reason DF Legends never claims to know what a world has not said.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>